.venv-hpc/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
data/raw/
data/processed/
runs/
*.egg-info/
.env

# The authoritative cluster results for the GB1 sweep, recovered from Slurm stdout.
# runs/ is otherwise untracked, but this is the only record of the figures the Week 4
# debrief quotes, and local re-runs do not reproduce all of them (see ARCHITECTURE.md).
!runs/binding_cluster_finals.csv

# The agent-policy comparison on the GB1 pilot: the arm Slurm job 19202 never ran.
# runs/ is otherwise untracked, but this is the only record that the LLM policy was
# measured against the heuristics, and the conclusion is a negative worth keeping.
!runs/agent_policy_comparison.csv
runs/twins/
runs/orbit/
runs/monomers/
runs/monitor/
runs/improve/

# The coverage-channel experiment: whether equalising axis coverage removes the advantage a
# policy gets from counting offers. runs/ is otherwise untracked, but this is the only record
# that the obvious repair was tried and does not work -- it relocates the advantage into
# dossier order rather than closing it -- and a repair that looks right and is not is exactly
# the thing a later reader would otherwise redo.
#
# Note on the three negations in this file: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, and `runs/` on line 6 excludes all three. They were added with
# `git add -f` and stay tracked because gitignore does not apply to tracked files. The
# negations are a record of intent, not the mechanism, and a fresh clone that deletes one of
# these will not get it back by rerunning anything.
!runs/coverage_channel.json

# Genome-to-ranked-targets, validated on three virus families with the pathogen held out of
# the reference each time. runs/ is otherwise untracked, but this is the record that the
# ranking recovers the targets with drugs against them across coronavirus, paramyxovirus and
# orthomyxovirus rather than on the one family it was built against.
!runs/intake_validation.json

# The holdout ladder: how distant the nearest curated relative may be before identification
# stops. runs/ is otherwise untracked, but this is the record that the validation above is an
# isolate holdout rather than a species one, and that one rung further out the pipeline
# returns nothing. A limit nobody measured would be assumed to be further away than it is.
!runs/holdout_ladder.json

# The three-tier identification cascade: what is recoverable past the cliff the ladder found,
# and by which mechanism. runs/ is otherwise untracked, but this is the record that conserved
# enzymes survive cross-family homology while surface antigens do not and must be recovered
# from their own sequence instead.
!runs/identification_cascade.json

# Cross-kingdom transfer: the same pipeline on a bacterial genome, with M. tuberculosis held
# out. runs/ is otherwise untracked, but this records that identification and ranking transfer
# from viruses while six-frame calling and length ranking do not, and that all four first-line
# TB drug target complexes land in the top 2.3 percent of 4,085 predicted genes.
!runs/cross_kingdom_intake.json

# Drug-target ranks against pathogen genome input, one row per target, with the denominator
# and the rank-sum probability on every row. runs/ is otherwise untracked, but this is the
# deliverable the collaborator reads and the record that the ranking beats chance on three of
# four pathogens and not on Nipah.
!runs/target_ranks.csv

# Surface markers scored the way a macrocycle sees a target, with the contact-cutoff
# sensitivity beside them. runs/ is otherwise untracked, but this is the record that scoring
# a contiguous hydrophobic patch ranks a flat interface above a deep enzyme pocket, which is
# the reverse of a small-molecule druggability score and the right way round here.
!runs/surface_markers.json

# The attempt to score on those markers, and why it was withdrawn. runs/ is otherwise
# untracked, but a change that was measured, made the ranking worse in two different forms and
# was reverted is exactly the record a later reader needs in order not to retry it.
!runs/surface_in_ranker.json

# The macrocycle-amenability gate and why its validation is inconclusive. runs/ is otherwise
# untracked, but a result recorded as inconclusive, with the two defects that made it so, is
# worth more than the apparent agreement it would otherwise have reported.
!runs/amenability_gate.json
.venv-pfn/

# The notebook points MPLCONFIGDIR here so a stale user-level matplotlibrc cannot print a
# backend warning into a demo. It is a cache, never a record.
notebooks/.mplcache/
.mplcache/
notebooks/.ipynb_checkpoints/
